      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Vandegrift graveyard, laid out in 1775 on a 214‑acre tract granted in 1697, is an ancient landmark of Cornwells Heights.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://pennsylvaniagenealogy.org/bucks/cornwells-heights-pennsylvania.htm",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Halfway House, first licensed to John Vandegrift in 1744, has been a famous hotel in Cornwells since that time.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
